rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，抽象类应该包含至少一个抽象方法来让其子类进行实现。那些没有任何抽象方法的抽象类可能会导致代码混淆，降低代码的清晰度和可维护性。

##### 规则意义
当抽象类没有抽象方法时，其存在的意义将受到质疑，因此建议避免创建这种类。这样可以保持代码的简洁性和可读性，同时确保类型的明确性。

##### 错误示例
```java
abstract class MyEmptyAbstractClass {
    // 无抽象方法
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
abstract class MyAbstractClass {
    abstract void myAbstractMethod(); // 包含抽象方法
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, an abstract class should contain at least one abstract method for its subclasses to implement. An abstract class without any abstract methods may lead to confusion in the code and reduce its clarity and maintainability.

##### Rule Significance
When an abstract class does not have abstract methods, its existence will be questioned, so it is advisable to avoid creating such classes. This helps maintain the simplicity and readability of the code, while ensuring the clarity of types.

##### Error Example
```java
abstract class MyEmptyAbstractClass {
    // No abstract methods
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
abstract class MyAbstractClass {
    abstract void myAbstractMethod(); // Contains an abstract method
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在确保在Java类中生成合适的访问器类，以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 规则意义
遵循这一规则可以帮助开发者在创建Java类时生成标准化的访问器，避免不必要的错误和混淆，从而提升代码的整体质量和结构。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
    // 缺少访问器方法
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to ensure the generation of appropriate accessor methods in Java classes to improve code readability and maintainability.

##### Rule Significance
Adhering to this rule can assist developers in creating standardized accessors when designing Java classes, avoiding unnecessary errors and confusion, thereby enhancing the overall quality and structure of the code.

##### Error Example
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
    // Missing accessor method
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }
    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检查类中是否缺少生成访问器方法（getter和setter）。

##### 规则意义
访问器方法是对象属性访问的标准方法，缺少这些方法可能导致代码的封装性降低，增加了对类内部实现的依赖，从而影响代码的可维护性和可扩展性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        this.age = age;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for the absence of accessor methods (getters and setters) in a class.

##### Rule Significance
Accessor methods are the standard way to access object properties. The absence of these methods may lead to reduced encapsulation in the code, increasing dependency on the internal implementation of the class, which in turn affects the maintainability and extensibility of the code.

##### Error Example
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getAge() {
        return age;
    }

    public void setAge(int age) {
        this.age = age;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在防止在代码中不必要地添加空字符串，例如 `""`，这可能导致代码在可读性和维护性方面的负担。

##### 规则意义
添加空字符串通常没有实际意义，这可能会造成混淆，并降低代码的可读性和可维护性。开发者应该避免使用空字符串，而代之以更明确的处理方式。

##### 错误示例
```java
String str = "";
if (str.equals("")) {
    // 处理空字符串的逻辑
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
// 使用null或明确的字符串处理
String str = null;
if (str == null) {
    // 处理null情况
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to prevent the unnecessary addition of empty strings in code, such as `""`, which can lead to a burden on readability and maintainability.

##### Rule Significance
Adding empty strings often holds no practical meaning, which can cause confusion and reduce the readability and maintainability of the code. Developers should avoid using empty strings and instead opt for more explicit handling approaches.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
String str = "";
if (str.equals("")) {
    // Logic for handling empty string
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
// Use null or explicit string handling
String str = null;
if (str == null) {
    // Handle null case
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测字符串拼接时使用字符而非字符数组或字符串构建块的情况。

##### 规则意义
在Java中，直接使用字符进行字符串拼接可能会导致性能问题，因为每次拼接都会创建新的字符串对象。建议使用`StringBuilder`或`StringBuffer`来提高效率。

##### 错误示例
'''java
char c1 = 'H';
char c2 = 'i';
String result = c1 + c2; // 不推荐
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
char c1 = 'H';
char c2 = 'i';
String result = String.valueOf(c1) + c2; // 或者使用StringBuilder
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
sb.append(c1).append(c2);
String result = sb.toString(); // 推荐使用
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect cases where characters are used for string concatenation instead of character arrays or string building blocks.

##### Rule Meaning
In Java, directly using characters for string concatenation may lead to performance issues because a new string object is created with each concatenation. It is recommended to use `StringBuilder` or `StringBuffer` for better efficiency.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
char c1 = 'H';
char c2 = 'i';
String result = c1 + c2; // Not recommended
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
char c1 = 'H';
char c2 = 'i';
String result = String.valueOf(c1) + c2; // Or use StringBuilder
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
sb.append(c1).append(c2);
String result = sb.toString(); // Recommended
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，数组不应直接存储在数据结构中，而应使用集合类（如ArrayList）来代替。

##### 规则意义
直接存储数组可能导致灵活性降低，增加对数组大小和类型的依赖，进而影响代码的可维护性和可扩展性。使用集合类可以更好地管理元素，允许动态调整大小。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private int[] numbers = new int[10]; // 直接使用数组
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    private List<Integer> numbers = new ArrayList<>(); // 使用集合类
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, arrays should not be stored directly in data structures; instead, collection classes (such as ArrayList) should be used.

##### Rule Meaning
Directly storing arrays may lead to reduced flexibility, increased dependency on the size and type of the arrays, which can affect the maintainability and scalability of the code. Using collection classes allows for better management of elements and enables dynamic resizing.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    private int[] numbers = new int[10]; // Directly using an array
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    private List<Integer> numbers = new ArrayList<>(); // Using a collection class
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在表达式中使用赋值操作符可能导致代码逻辑错误，并且使代码的可读性下降。

##### 规则意义
使用赋值语句(如 `=`) 的同时又作为操作数，可能会导致意料之外的结果，增加代码出错的风险。此规则旨在提醒开发者避免在表达式中使用赋值操作。

##### 错误示例
```java
int x = 10;
if (x = 5) { // 这里应使用==进行比较
    System.out.println("x 是 5");
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
int x = 10;
if (x == 5) { // 使用相等运算符进行比较
    System.out.println("x 是 5");
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using the assignment operator in expressions may lead to logical errors in the code and decrease code readability.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using assignment statements (such as `=`) as operands may result in unexpected outcomes, increasing the risk of errors in the code. This rule aims to remind developers to avoid using assignment operations in expressions.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
int x = 10;
if (x = 5) { // Should use == for comparison here
    System.out.println("x is 5");
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
int x = 10;
if (x == 5) { // Use equality operator for comparison
    System.out.println("x is 5");
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测在非最终(static)静态变量上进行赋值的操作，可能导致不可预期的行为或程序状态。

##### 规则意义
静态变量如果被多次修改，可能会影响多个对象的行为和状态，这在并发环境下尤其危险。避免对非最终的静态变量进行赋值可以提高代码的可预测性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private static int count;

    public void increment() {
        count++; // 错误: 非最终静态变量被赋值
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    private static final int COUNT = 0;

    public void increment() {
        // 正确: 不对非最终静态变量进行赋值
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects assignments to non-final (static) static variables, which may lead to unpredictable behavior or program state.

##### Rule Meaning
If static variables are modified multiple times, they can affect the behavior and state of multiple objects, which is particularly dangerous in concurrent environments. Avoiding assignments to non-final static variables can improve the predictability and maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    private static int count;

    public void increment() {
        count++; // Error: Non-final static variable assigned
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    private static final int COUNT = 0;

    public void increment() {
        // Correct: No assignment to non-final static variable
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则要求每个类至少提供一个构造函数。如果类没有定义任何构造函数，编译器会自动生成一个默认构造函数，但这可能导致意外的行为，尤其是在类中有其他成员变量时。

##### 规则意义
确保每个类都有明确的构造函数，可以提高代码可读性和可维护性，减少构造对象时可能产生的错误。同时，显式定义构造函数也有助于保证对象在创建时以一个有效的状态进行初始化。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private int number;
    // 缺少构造函数
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    private int number;

    // 定义构造函数
    public Example(int number) {
        this.number = number;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule requires every class to provide at least one constructor. If a class does not define any constructors, the compiler will automatically generate a default constructor, but this can lead to unintended behavior, especially when there are other member variables in the class.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that every class has a clear constructor can improve code readability and maintainability, reducing the potential for errors during object creation. Additionally, explicitly defining constructors helps ensure that objects are initialized in a valid state when created.

##### Error Example
```java
public class Example {
    private int number;
    // Missing constructor
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    private int number;

    // Define constructor
    public Example(int number) {
        this.number = number;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，访问修饰符用于控制类、方法和变量的可见性。当我们不小心更改了访问修饰符的可见性时，可能会影响到类的外部使用和继承，从而导致意想不到的错误。

##### 规则意义
遵循这一规则可以确保代码在修改后仍然保持与外部系统的兼容性，并避免潜在的安全隐患和程序错误。

##### 错误示例
```java
class Example {
    protected void method() {
        // 原本是 protected 方法
    }
}

class SubExample extends Example {
    public void method() {  // 错误：将访问修饰符从 protected 修改为 public
        // 覆盖父类的方法
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
class Example {
    protected void method() {
        // 保持访问修饰符不变
    }
}

class SubExample extends Example {
    @Override
    protected void method() {  // 正确：保持访问修饰符为 protected
        // 覆盖父类的方法
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, access modifiers are used to control the visibility of classes, methods, and variables. When we inadvertently change the visibility of an access modifier, it may affect external usage and inheritance of the class, leading to unexpected errors.

##### Rule Significance
Following this rule ensures that the code remains compatible with external systems after modifications and avoids potential security risks and program errors.

##### Error Example
```java
class Example {
    protected void method() {
        // Originally a protected method
    }
}

class SubExample extends Example {
    public void method() {  // Error: Changing access modifier from protected to public
        // Overriding the parent class method
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
class Example {
    protected void method() {
        // Keep the access modifier unchanged
    }
}

class SubExample extends Example {
    @Override
    protected void method() {  // Correct: Keeping the access modifier as protected
        // Overriding the parent class method
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在代码中应该尽量避免使用数组的循环，尤其是嵌套循环。这种做法可能导致性能问题，尤其是在处理大数据集时。

##### 规则意义
使用数组循环可能会影响代码的可读性和维护性，并且在性能上可能造成不必要的开销，特别是对于大型数组。当存在多个数组层次的循环时，性能影响更加显著。因此，建议开发者使用其他更高效的数据结构或算法来替代数组循环。

##### 错误示例
```java
for (int i = 0; i < array1.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < array2.length; j++) {
        // 对每个元素进行处理
        process(array1[i], array2[j]);
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
// 使用流处理替代数组循环
Arrays.stream(array1).forEach(a -> Arrays.stream(array2).forEach(b -> process(a, b)));
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Avoid using array loops in the code as much as possible, especially nested loops. This practice may lead to performance issues, particularly when handling large datasets.

##### Rule Significance
Using array loops can affect the readability and maintainability of the code, and it may cause unnecessary overhead in terms of performance, especially for large arrays. When there are multiple levels of nested loops with arrays, the performance impact becomes even more significant. Therefore, it is recommended that developers use other more efficient data structures or algorithms as alternatives to array loops.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
for (int i = 0; i < array1.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < array2.length; j++) {
        // Process each element
        process(array1[i], array2[j]);
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
// Use stream processing instead of array loops
Arrays.stream(array1).forEach(a -> Arrays.stream(array2).forEach(b -> process(a, b)));
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在循环的最后一条语句中使用分支语句（如 `if` 或 `switch`）可能会导致代码逻辑复杂且不易理解。这种写法可能隐藏bug或导致不必要的代码执行。

##### 规则意义
使用分支语句可能导致意外的控制流，增加了代码的复杂性，降低了代码的可读性和可维护性。因此，应尽量避免在循环的最后使用分支语句。

##### 错误示例
'''java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    // 做一些工作
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        System.out.println(i);
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    // 做一些工作
}
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        System.out.println(i);
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using branching statements (such as `if` or `switch`) at the end of a loop can lead to complex and hard-to-understand code logic. This practice may hide bugs or cause unnecessary code execution.

##### Rule Meaning
Using branching statements may result in unexpected control flow, increasing code complexity and reducing code readability and maintainability. Therefore, it is advisable to avoid using branching statements at the end of loops.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    // Do some work
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        System.out.println(i);
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    // Do some work
}
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        System.out.println(i);
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在避免使用`Calendar`类来创建日期，因为`Calendar`类的设计复杂，且易于产生错误。

##### 规则意义
`Calendar`类在创建日期时不仅冗长，而且由于其复杂性，容易导致逻辑错误。Java 8引入了`java.time`包，提供了更简洁和清晰的日期和时间API，建议使用`LocalDate`, `LocalDateTime`等替代`Calendar`。

##### 错误示例
'''java
import java.util.Calendar;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Calendar calendar = Calendar.getInstance();
        calendar.set(2023, 0, 31); // 问题：使用Calendar创建日期
        System.out.println(calendar.getTime());
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
import java.time.LocalDate;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LocalDate date = LocalDate.of(2023, 1, 31); // 正确：使用LocalDate创建日期
        System.out.println(date);
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to avoid using the `Calendar` class to create dates because the design of the `Calendar` class is complex and prone to errors.

##### Rule Meaning
The `Calendar` class is not only verbose when creating dates, but its complexity can also lead to logical errors. Java 8 introduced the `java.time` package, which provides a more concise and clearer date and time API. It is recommended to use `LocalDate`, `LocalDateTime`, and others as alternatives to `Calendar`.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
import java.util.Calendar;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Calendar calendar = Calendar.getInstance();
        calendar.set(2023, 0, 31); // Problem: creating date using Calendar
        System.out.println(calendar.getTime());
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
import java.time.LocalDate;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LocalDate date = LocalDate.of(2023, 1, 31); // Correct: creating date using LocalDate
        System.out.println(date);
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 Java 中，`finalize` 方法用于清理资源，但是其使用已经不再推荐，因为它的执行时机不可靠，可能导致内存泄漏或预测不到的行为。

##### 规则意义
调用 `finalize` 方法可能导致资源无法及时释放，并且不确定执行时机，影响程序的性能和稳定性。Java 9 及其之后的版本更推荐使用 `java.lang.ref.Cleaner` 或其他资源管理方式。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class MyClass {
    protected void finalize() throws Throwable {
        try {
            // 资源清理工作
        } finally {
            super.finalize();
        }
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class MyClass {
    private final Cleaner cleaner = Cleaner.create();

    public MyClass() {
        // 注册清理工作
        cleaner.register(this, new State());
    }

    private static class State implements Runnable {
        @Override
        public void run() {
            // 资源清理工作
        }
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, the `finalize` method is used for resource cleanup, but its use is no longer recommended due to its unreliable execution timing, which can lead to memory leaks or unpredictable behavior.

##### Rule Importance
Calling the `finalize` method can result in resources not being released in a timely manner and the execution timing being uncertain, affecting the performance and stability of the program. Java 9 and later versions recommend using `java.lang.ref.Cleaner` or other resource management methods instead.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class MyClass {
    protected void finalize() throws Throwable {
        try {
            // Resource cleanup work
        } finally {
            super.finalize();
        }
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class MyClass {
    private final Cleaner cleaner = Cleaner.create();

    public MyClass() {
        // Register cleanup work
        cleaner.register(this, new State());
    }

    private static class State implements Runnable {
        @Override
        public void run() {
            // Resource cleanup work
        }
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在避免在代码中捕获通用异常（`Exception`），因为这样可能会掩盖其他潜在的异常问题。

##### 规则意义
捕获通用异常将导致开发者不明确地处理具体异常情况，也使得排查故障时更加困难。因此，应尽量捕获具体的异常类型，以便更准确地了解错误的原因并进行相应处理。

##### 错误示例
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出多种异常的代码
} catch (Exception e) {
    // 捕获通用异常
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出多种异常的代码
} catch (IOException e) {
    // 处理特定的IOException
    e.printStackTrace();
} catch (SQLException e) {
    // 处理特定的SQLException
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to avoid catching general exceptions (`Exception`) in code, as this may obscure other potential exception issues.

##### Significance of the Rule
Catching general exceptions leads developers to handle specific exception cases ambiguously, making it more difficult to troubleshoot issues. Therefore, it is advisable to catch specific exception types to better understand the cause of errors and handle them appropriately.

##### Error Example
```java
try {
    // Code that may throw various exceptions
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Catching a general exception
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
try {
    // Code that may throw various exceptions
} catch (IOException e) {
    // Handling a specific IOException
    e.printStackTrace();
} catch (SQLException e) {
    // Handling a specific SQLException
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
避免捕获空指针异常（NullPointerException），因为这通常意味着程序存在逻辑错误，而不是一种可预见的异常情况，捕获这种异常可能掩盖潜在的缺陷。

##### 规则意义
捕获空指针异常可能导致代码隐蔽的bug，增加了维护的复杂性。在处理可能为空的对象时，应该采取适当的防护措施，而不仅仅是通过捕获异常来处理。

##### 错误示例
```java
try {
    Object obj = null;
    obj.toString();
} catch (NullPointerException e) {
    // 不应该这样捕获
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
Object obj = null;
if (obj != null) {
    obj.toString();
} else {
    // 处理空对象的情况
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Avoid catching NullPointerException, as it typically indicates a logical error in the program rather than a foreseeable exceptional situation. Catching this exception may conceal potential defects.

##### Rule Significance
Catching NullPointerException can lead to hidden bugs in the code and increase the complexity of maintenance. Appropriate protective measures should be taken when dealing with potentially null objects, rather than merely handling the situation through exception catching.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
try {
    Object obj = null;
    obj.toString();
} catch (NullPointerException e) {
    // This is not how it should be caught
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
Object obj = null;
if (obj != null) {
    obj.toString();
} else {
    // Handle the case of the null object
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，捕获`Throwable`会导致捕获所有类型的异常，包括`Error`，这可能会掩盖真实的错误状态并导致应用程序的不稳定。

##### 规则意义
为了提高代码的健壮性和可维护性，应该避免捕获`Throwable`，而应捕获具体的异常类型（如`Exception`或其子类），这样可以更明确地处理不同类型的异常。

##### 错误示例
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (Throwable t) {
    // 不推荐的做法：捕获所有Throwable
    t.printStackTrace();
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (Exception e) {
    // 推荐做法：捕获具体的异常类型
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, catching `Throwable` will result in catching all types of exceptions, including `Error`, which may obscure the real error state and lead to application instability.

##### Rule Significance
To improve the robustness and maintainability of the code, one should avoid catching `Throwable` and instead catch specific types of exceptions (such as `Exception` or its subclasses) to handle different types of exceptions more explicitly.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
try {
    // Code that may throw an exception
} catch (Throwable t) {
    // Not recommended: catching all Throwable
    t.printStackTrace();
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
try {
    // Code that may throw an exception
} catch (Exception e) {
    // Recommended: catching specific types of exceptions
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
深度嵌套的if语句会导致代码可读性差和维护困难。此规则建议尽量减少if语句的嵌套层级。

##### 规则意义
深层嵌套的if语句不仅使代码难以理解，还增加了出错的几率和维护的复杂性。通过限制嵌套层级，可以提高代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''java
if (condition1) {
    if (condition2) {
        if (condition3) {
            // 业务逻辑
        }
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
if (condition1 && condition2 && condition3) {
    // 业务逻辑
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Deeply nested if statements lead to poor code readability and maintenance difficulties. This rule advises minimizing the levels of nested if statements.

##### Rule significance
Deeply nested if statements not only make the code hard to understand, but also increase the likelihood of errors and the complexity of maintenance. By limiting the levels of nesting, the readability and maintainability of the code can be improved.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
if (condition1) {
    if (condition2) {
        if (condition3) {
            // Business logic
        }
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
if (condition1 && condition2 && condition3) {
    // Business logic
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java代码中，避免使用美元符号（$）作为标识符的组成部分。这是因为美元符号容易引起混淆，并可能影响代码的可读性。

##### 规则意义
使用美元符号可能导致代码可读性降低，特别是在大型项目中，可能让团队成员难以理解代码的结构和意图。保持一致的命名风格有助于提高代码的维护性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example$Class {
    private int value;

    public Example$Class(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class ExampleClass {
    private int value;

    public ExampleClass(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java code, avoid using the dollar sign ($) as part of an identifier. This is because the dollar sign can lead to confusion and may affect the readability of the code.

##### Rule Meaning
Using the dollar sign may reduce code readability, especially in large projects, potentially making it difficult for team members to understand the structure and intent of the code. Maintaining a consistent naming style helps improve the maintainability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example$Class {
    private int value;

    public Example$Class(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class ExampleClass {
    private int value;

    public ExampleClass(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在代码中避免使用重复的字符串字面量，以减少内存使用并避免潜在的错误。

##### 规则意义
重复的字面量可能会导致代码可读性下降，并且在需要修改某个字面量时，可能会遗漏某一个实例从而导致潜在的缺陷。通过使用常量，开发者可以提高代码的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''java
public class Sample {
    public void demo() {
        String greeting = "Hello";
        System.out.println("Hello");  // 重复字面量
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
public class Sample {
    private static final String GREETING = "Hello";

    public void demo() {
        System.out.println(GREETING);  // 使用常量
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Avoid using duplicate string literals in code to reduce memory usage and prevent potential errors.

##### Rule Meaning
Duplicate literals can decrease code readability, and when a modification of a literal is needed, a particular instance may be overlooked, leading to potential defects. By using constants, developers can improve the maintainability and readability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
public class Sample {
    public void demo() {
        String greeting = "Hello";
        System.out.println("Hello");  // Duplicate literal
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
public class Sample {
    private static final String GREETING = "Hello";

    public void demo() {
        System.out.println(GREETING);  // Using constant
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在防止使用枚举类型作为标识符，避免可能的命名冲突和代码可读性问题。

##### 规则意义
在Java中，使用枚举作为标识符可能导致代码的不必要复杂性，增加了理解和维护的难度。遵循此规则可以确保代码的清晰性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
