This rule aims to prevent the use of enumeration types as identifiers to avoid potential naming conflicts and issues with code readability.

##### Rule Significance
In Java, using enumerations as identifiers can lead to unnecessary complexity in the code, increasing the difficulty of understanding and maintaining it. Adhering to this rule ensures clarity and readability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
enum Color {
    RED, GREEN, BLUE
}

public class Example {
