}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
public void processResult() {
    SomeObject result = getResult();
    if (result != null) { // Check if the result is null
        result.doSomething();
    } else {
        // Handle the case where the result is null
        handleNullResult();
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在使用 `toArray()` 方法时，如果提供了不正确的数组类型，可能会导致 `ClassCastException`。该规则旨在提醒开发者注意避免这种潜在的运行时异常。

##### 规则意义
使用 `toArray()` 方法时，如果给定的数组类型与集合中的元素类型不一致，Java 会在运行时抛出 `ClassCastException`。这可能导致应用程序崩溃或不可预期的行为。因此，开发者需要确保在调用 `toArray()` 时传入正确的数组类型。

##### 错误示例
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add("Hello");
        list.add("World");

        // 错误示例：传入不正确类型的数组会导致 ClassCastException
        Integer[] array = list.toArray(new Integer[0]); // ClassCastException
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add("Hello");
        list.add("World");

        // 正确示例：传入相同类型的数组，不会导致异常
        String[] array = list.toArray(new String[0]);
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using the `toArray()` method, providing an incorrect array type may lead to a `ClassCastException`. This rule aims to alert developers to avoid this potential runtime exception.

##### Rule Significance
When using the `toArray()` method, if the given array type is inconsistent with the element type in the collection, Java will throw a `ClassCastException` at runtime. This can result in application crashes or unexpected behavior. Therefore, developers need to ensure that the correct array type is passed when calling `toArray()`.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add("Hello");
        list.add("World");

        // Incorrect Example: Passing an array of the wrong type will cause ClassCastException
        Integer[] array = list.toArray(new Integer[0]); // ClassCastException
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class Example {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add("Hello");
        list.add("World");

        // Correct Example: Passing an array of the same type will not cause an exception
        String[] array = list.toArray(new String[0]);
    }
}
```

