rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，克隆方法用于复制对象。为了确保对象能够正确地被克隆，克隆方法应该是公共的。

##### 规则意义
如果克隆方法不是公共的，外部代码将无法访问该方法，从而无法进行对象复制，这可能导致意外行为并影响程序的可用性。

##### 错误示例
```java
class Example {
    protected Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
class Example implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, the clone method is used to copy objects. To ensure that an object can be cloned correctly, the clone method should be public.

##### Rule Meaning
If the clone method is not public, external code will not be able to access this method, which prevents object copying and may lead to unexpected behavior, affecting the usability of the program.

##### Error Example
```java
class Example {
    protected Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
class Example implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，如果类实现了`clone()`方法，那么它应该也实现`Cloneable`接口。否则，在调用`clone()`方法时将会抛出`CloneNotSupportedException`，这将导致代码的潜在错误。

##### 规则意义
确保类在进行克隆时提供正确的支持，以便使用者可以安全地调用`clone()`方法而不会遇到运行时异常。实现`Cloneable`接口表明该类的实例可以被克隆，符合程序员的期望。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    protected Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, if a class implements the `clone()` method, it should also implement the `Cloneable` interface. Otherwise, calling the `clone()` method will throw a `CloneNotSupportedException`, which can lead to potential errors in the code.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that the class provides the correct support for cloning so that users can safely call the `clone()` method without encountering runtime exceptions. Implementing the `Cloneable` interface indicates that instances of the class can be cloned, aligning with the expectations of programmers.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    public Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example implements Cloneable {
    @Override
    protected Object clone() throws CloneNotSupportedException {
        return super.clone();
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
克隆方法的返回类型应与其所属的类名相匹配，以确保类型安全和一致性。

##### 规则意义
克隆方法通常用于创建对象的副本，如果返回类型不匹配，可能导致向上转型错误，影响程序的可维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
```java
class MyClass {
    public Object clone() {
        return new MyClass();
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
class MyClass {
    @Override
    public MyClass clone() {
        return new MyClass();
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
The return type of the clone method should match the name of its class to ensure type safety and consistency.

##### Significance of the Rule
The clone method is typically used to create a copy of an object; if the return type does not match, it may lead to upcasting errors, affecting the maintainability and readability of the program.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
class MyClass {
    public Object clone() {
        return new MyClass();
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
class MyClass {
    @Override
    public MyClass clone() {
        return new MyClass();
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，未关闭的资源可能导致内存泄漏或其他不必要的资源占用。使用完资源后，务必及时关闭它们，以确保系统性能和稳定性。

##### 规则意义
及时关闭资源（如文件、数据库连接、网络连接等）能够避免资源泄露，维护应用程序的性能和可靠性。未关闭的资源可能会导致系统变得不稳定，甚至出现崩溃情况。

##### 错误示例
'''java
FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("example.txt");
byte[] data = new byte[100];
fis.read(data);
// 资源未关闭导致潜在泄漏
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
FileInputStream fis = null;
try {
    fis = new FileInputStream("example.txt");
    byte[] data = new byte[100];
    fis.read(data);
} finally {
    if (fis != null) {
        try {
            fis.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, unclosed resources can lead to memory leaks or other unnecessary resource usage. It is essential to close resources promptly after use to ensure system performance and stability.

##### Rule Significance
Timely closing of resources (such as files, database connections, network connections, etc.) can prevent resource leaks and maintain the application's performance and reliability. Unclosed resources may cause the system to become unstable and may even lead to crashes.

##### Error Example
'''java
FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("example.txt");
byte[] data = new byte[100];
fis.read(data);
// Resource not closed, leading to potential leakage
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
FileInputStream fis = null;
try {
    fis = new FileInputStream("example.txt");
    byte[] data = new byte[100];
    fis.read(data);
} finally {
    if (fis != null) {
        try {
            fis.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
本规则旨在检测代码的认知复杂度，复杂度越高，代码的可理解性和可维护性通常越低。

##### 规则意义
认知复杂度是衡量代码可读性和可维护性的一个重要指标。过高的认知复杂度可能导致理解困难，从而增加了错误发生的风险，并降低代码的可维护性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public void process(Order order) {
    if (order != null) {
        if (order.isValid()) {
            if (order.hasItems()) {
                // 处理有效订单
            } else {
                // 报告错误：订单没有项目
            }
        } else {
            // 报告错误：订单无效
        }
    } else {
        // 报告错误：订单为空
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public void process(Order order) {
    if (order == null) {
        // 报告错误：订单为空
        return;
    }
    if (!order.isValid()) {
        // 报告错误：订单无效
        return;
    }
    if (!order.hasItems()) {
        // 报告错误：订单没有项目
        return;
    }
    // 处理有效订单
}
```

