rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在类、方法和属性中缺乏对默认访问修饰符的注释，会导致代码可读性降低，难以理解其可见性。

##### 规则意义
明确标识默认的访问修饰符，可以提高代码的可维护性，并帮助其他开发者更容易理解代码的意图。默认访问修饰符的使用需要有意识地进行管理，以避免不必要的访问控制混乱。

##### 错误示例
```java
class MyClass {
    int myVariable; // 默认访问修饰符未注释

    void myMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
class MyClass {
    /**
     * 默认访问修饰符，允许同一包内的访问
     */
    int myVariable; // 默认访问修饰符是包级私有

    /**
     * 默认访问修饰符，允许同一包内的访问
     */
    void myMethod() {
        // 方法实现
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
The absence of comments regarding default access modifiers in classes, methods, and properties can lead to reduced code readability and difficulty in understanding their visibility.

##### Significance of the Rule
Clearly identifying default access modifiers can enhance code maintainability and help other developers more easily understand the intent of the code. The use of default access modifiers needs to be consciously managed to avoid unnecessary confusion in access control.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
class MyClass {
    int myVariable; // Default access modifier not commented

    void myMethod() {
        // Method implementation
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
class MyClass {
    /**
     * Default access modifier, allows access within the same package
     */
    int myVariable; // Default access modifier is package-private

    /**
     * Default access modifier, allows access within the same package
     */
    void myMethod() {
        // Method implementation
    }
}
```

