#### 规则概述
此规则旨在确保应用程序中的操作是幂等的，即无论执行多少次，结果都应该是相同的。为了确保系统在重复执行相同操作时的稳定性和一致性，确保幂等性是重要的设计原则。

##### 规则意义
幂等性是分布式系统设计中的一个重要特性，它可以防止因为网络请求重复导致的状态不一致或错误。确保操作的幂等性能够提高系统的健壮性，减少错误发生的几率。

##### 错误示例
```java
public void updateUser(User user) {
    // 此操作不是幂等的，会导致重复更新，因此可能会产生错误
    user.update();  // 假设这是一个更新操作
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public void updateUser(User user) {
    // 确保使用幂等操作进行更新，检查用户状态再决定是否进行更新
    if (!user.isUpdated()) {
        user.update();
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that operations in the application are idempotent, meaning that no matter how many times they are executed, the results should be the same. Ensuring idempotency is an important design principle to guarantee the stability and consistency of the system during repeated execution of the same operation.

##### Significance of the Rule
Idempotency is an important characteristic in the design of distributed systems, as it can prevent state inconsistencies or errors caused by repeated network requests. Ensuring the idempotency of operations can enhance the robustness of the system and reduce the likelihood of errors occurring.

##### Error Example
```java
public void updateUser(User user) {
    // This operation is not idempotent and may lead to repeated updates, potentially causing errors
    user.update();  // Assume this is an update operation
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public void updateUser(User user) {
    // Ensure to use an idempotent operation for updates, check the user status before deciding to update
    if (!user.isUpdated()) {
        user.update();
    }
}
```

