##### Error Example
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (IOException | SQLException e) {
    System.out.println("处理 IOException 或 SQLException");
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("处理通用异常");
} catch (IOException e) {
    System.out.println("处理 IOException");
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
try {
    // 可能抛出异常的代码
} catch (IOException | SQLException e) {
    System.out.println("处理 IOException 或 SQLException");
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("处理通用异常");
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
本规则旨在确保类中的字段被定义为不可变，以提高代码的安全性与可维护性。不可变字段通常被定义为`final`，并且在构造对象后不会改变。

##### 规则意义
不可变字段可以防止多人同时对同一对象进行修改，减少潜在的bug，同时提高代码的可读性和可测试性。通过确保某些关键字段为不可变，可以使得类的行为更加一致。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private String name;

    public Example(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name; // 这里允许修改字段，违反不可变性
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    private final String name;

    public Example(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name; // 不允许修改字段，保持不可变性
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that fields in a class are defined as immutable, enhancing the security and maintainability of the code. Immutable fields are typically defined as `final` and will not change after the object is constructed.

##### Significance of the Rule
Immutable fields can prevent multiple users from modifying the same object simultaneously, reducing potential bugs, while also improving the readability and testability of the code. By ensuring that certain key fields are immutable, the behavior of the class can be made more consistent.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    private String name;

    public Example(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name; // Allows modification of the field, violating immutability
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    private final String name;

    public Example(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name; // Does not allow modification of the field, maintaining immutability
    }
}
```

