This rule checks whether developers are using implicit functional interfaces, that is, interfaces that are not explicitly declared as functional interfaces but still meet the definition of a functional interface.

##### Rule Meaning
Using implicit functional interfaces can lead to decreased code readability and may introduce unnecessary complexity in certain cases. Explicitly declaring an interface as a functional interface not only improves the readability of the code but also helps developers better understand the purpose of the interface.

