rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测到在switch语句中未使用break或return语句，导致多个case之间隐式穿透。

##### 规则意义
隐式穿透可能导致程序逻辑错误，使得某个case意外地执行了下一个case的逻辑，从而引发难以发现的缺陷或一致性问题。明确地使用break可以使代码更易于理解和维护。

##### 错误示例
```java
switch (value) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Case 1");
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Case 2");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Case 3");
        break;
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
switch (value) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Case 1");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Case 2");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Case 3");
        break;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects the absence of break or return statements in switch statements, leading to implicit fall-through between multiple cases.

##### Rule Meaning
Implicit fall-through can cause logical errors in the program, allowing a particular case to unexpectedly execute the logic of the next case, potentially resulting in hard-to-detect defects or consistency issues. Clearly using break statements can make the code easier to understand and maintain.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
switch (value) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Case 1");
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Case 2");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Case 3");
        break;
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
switch (value) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Case 1");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Case 2");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Case 3");
        break;
}
```

