#### 规则概述
在JUnit4测试中，建议使用@Before注解来初始化每个测试用例所需的共享资源。

##### 规则意义
通过使用@Before注解，可以避免代码重复，提高代码的可维护性和可读性。这样，如果初始化逻辑需要更改，只需在一个地方进行修改，避免了在每个测试方法中重复编写初始化代码。

##### 错误示例
```java
import org.junit.Test;

public class ExampleTest {
    @Test
    public void testMethod1() {
        // 初始化共享资源
        SomeClass resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
        // 执行测试
        assertTrue(resource.someMethod());
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod2() {
        // 初始化共享资源
        SomeClass resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
        // 执行测试
        assertEquals(42, resource.someMethod());
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
import org.junit.Before;
import org.junit.Test;

public class ExampleTest {
    private SomeClass resource;

    @Before
    public void setUp() {
        // 在每个测试之前初始化共享资源
        resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod1() {
        // 执行测试
        assertTrue(resource.someMethod());
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod2() {
        // 执行测试
        assertEquals(42, resource.someMethod());
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In JUnit4 tests, it is recommended to use the @Before annotation to initialize shared resources required for each test case.

##### Rule Significance
By using the @Before annotation, you can avoid code duplication and improve the maintainability and readability of the code. This way, if the initialization logic needs to change, you only have to modify it in one place, avoiding the repetition of initialization code in each test method.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
import org.junit.Test;

public class ExampleTest {
    @Test
    public void testMethod1() {
        // Initialize shared resource
        SomeClass resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
        // Execute test
        assertTrue(resource.someMethod());
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod2() {
        // Initialize shared resource
        SomeClass resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
        // Execute test
        assertEquals(42, resource.someMethod());
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
import org.junit.Before;
import org.junit.Test;

public class ExampleTest {
    private SomeClass resource;

    @Before
    public void setUp() {
        // Initialize shared resource before each test
        resource = new SomeClass();
        resource.setup();
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod1() {
        // Execute test
        assertTrue(resource.someMethod());
    }

    @Test
    public void testMethod2() {
        // Execute test
        assertEquals(42, resource.someMethod());
    }
}
```

