'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to detect the use of confusing increment logic in increment operations, which may lead to unexpected behaviors and defects.

##### Rule Significance
Using multiple increment methods or transformations to update the same variable can lead to code that is difficult to read and maintain. Additionally, confusing increment methods may introduce subtle defects, making the code more prone to errors.

##### Error Example
'''java
