#### 规则概述
Loose package coupling 是一种设计原则，强调软件包之间应保持较低的耦合度，以提高代码的可维护性和可扩展性。

##### 规则意义
松散耦合的设计可以减少模块之间的依赖，使得模块更易于替换和重用，提升系统的整体灵活性和可测试性。过于紧密的耦合会导致修改一处代码时需修改多处代码，增加了维护难度。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class OrderService {
    private final UserService userService;
    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public OrderService() {
        this.userService = new UserService();
        this.paymentService = new PaymentService();
    }

    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        userService.validateUser(order.getUserId());
        paymentService.processPayment(order);
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class OrderService {
    private final UserService userService;
    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public OrderService(UserService userService, PaymentService paymentService) {
        this.userService = userService;
        this.paymentService = paymentService;
    }

    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        userService.validateUser(order.getUserId());
        paymentService.processPayment(order);
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Loose package coupling is a design principle that emphasizes maintaining a low coupling between packages to improve the maintainability and extensibility of the code.

##### Rule Significance
A loosely coupled design can reduce dependencies between modules, making them easier to replace and reuse, thereby enhancing the overall flexibility and testability of the system. Excessive tight coupling can result in having to modify multiple pieces of code when changing one, increasing maintenance difficulty.

##### Error Example
```java
public class OrderService {
    private final UserService userService;
    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public OrderService() {
        this.userService = new UserService();
        this.paymentService = new PaymentService();
    }

    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        userService.validateUser(order.getUserId());
        paymentService.processPayment(order);
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class OrderService {
    private final UserService userService;
    private final PaymentService paymentService;

    public OrderService(UserService userService, PaymentService paymentService) {
        this.userService = userService;
        this.paymentService = paymentService;
    }

    public void placeOrder(Order order) {
        userService.validateUser(order.getUserId());
        paymentService.processPayment(order);
    }
}
```

