#### 规则概述
该规则用于检测类中重写父类方法时是否缺少`@Override`注解。

##### 规则意义
使用`@Override`注解可以提高代码的可读性，避免因为方法签名的变更而导致的错误。缺少该注解可能会导致程序行为的不一致，难以被其他开发者发现。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Parent display");
    }
}

public class Child extends Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Child display");
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Parent display");
    }
}

public class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Child display");
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect whether the `@Override` annotation is missing when overriding a parent class method.

##### Rule Significance
The use of the `@Override` annotation can enhance code readability and prevent errors caused by changes in method signatures. Missing this annotation may lead to inconsistent program behavior that can be difficult for other developers to detect.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Parent display");
    }
}

public class Child extends Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Child display");
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Parent {
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Parent display");
    }
}

public class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    public void display() {
        System.out.println("Child display");
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
当一个类实现了Serializable接口，但没有定义serialVersionUID字段时，PMD会报告该问题。Java序列化是将对象状态转化为字节流的过程，serialVersionUID用于验证类的一致性。

##### 规则意义
缺失serialVersionUID在反序列化过程中可能导致InvalidClassException异常。如果没有定义serialVersionUID，Java会根据类的结构生成一个默认的ID，这在类的结构变化后可能导致不兼容的问题。

##### 错误示例
```java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class User implements Serializable {
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class User implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When a class implements the Serializable interface but does not define the serialVersionUID field, PMD will report this issue. Java serialization is the process of converting an object's state into a byte stream, and serialVersionUID is used to verify the consistency of a class.

##### Rule Significance
Missing serialVersionUID may lead to an InvalidClassException during the deserialization process. If serialVersionUID is not defined, Java will generate a default ID based on the class structure, which can lead to incompatibility issues after the class structure changes.

##### Error Example
```java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class User implements Serializable {
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class User implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    private String name;
    private int age;
}
```

