#### 规则概述
在类中使用可变的静态变量会导致状态共享的问题，从而引发多线程不安全或不可预测的行为。

##### 规则意义
使用可变的静态变量可能会在高并发环境下导致难以排查的错误和不一致的数据状态，影响程序的正确性和稳定性。建议将静态变量设为不可变，或者彻底避免使用可变的静态状态。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private static int counter = 0;

    public static void increment() {
        counter++;
    }

    public static int getCounter() {
        return counter;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    private static final int INITIAL_VALUE = 0;

    private Example() {}  // 防止实例化

    public static int getCounter() {
        return INITIAL_VALUE;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using mutable static variables in a class can lead to issues with state sharing, resulting in multithreading unsafety or unpredictable behavior.

##### Rule Meaning
Using mutable static variables can lead to hard-to-diagnose errors and inconsistent data states in high-concurrency environments, affecting the correctness and stability of the program. It is recommended to make static variables immutable or to completely avoid using mutable static states.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    private static int counter = 0;

    public static void increment() {
        counter++;
    }

    public static int getCounter() {
        return counter;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    private static final int INITIAL_VALUE = 0;

    private Example() {}  // Prevent instantiation

    public static int getCounter() {
        return INITIAL_VALUE;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
N路径复杂度是指程序的控制流图中所有可能的执行路径的数量。高N路径复杂度的代码可能会变得难以理解、测试和维护。

##### 规则意义
当代码的N路径复杂度过高时，可能导致以下问题：
- 代码的可测试性下降。
- 代码的可读性和可维护性降低。
- 难以识别代码中的潜在缺陷。

在设计和开发时，应尽量控制函数的复杂度，以确保代码的清晰性和简明性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    if (a > 0) {
        if (b > 0) {
            System.out.println("Both positive");
        } else {
            System.out.println("a is positive, b is not");
        }
    } else {
        if (b > 0) {
            System.out.println("a is not positive, b is");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Both not positive");
        }
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    String result;
    if (a > 0 && b > 0) {
        result = "Both positive";
    } else if (a > 0) {
        result = "a is positive, b is not";
    } else if (b > 0) {
        result = "a is not positive, b is";
    } else {
        result = "Both not positive";
    }
    System.out.println(result);
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
N-path complexity refers to the number of all possible execution paths in a program's control flow graph. Code with high N-path complexity can become difficult to understand, test, and maintain.

##### Rule Significance
When the N-path complexity of the code is too high, it may lead to the following issues:
- Decreased testability of the code.
- Reduced readability and maintainability of the code.
- Difficulty in identifying potential defects in the code.

During design and development, the complexity of functions should be minimized to ensure the clarity and conciseness of the code.

##### Error Example
```java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    if (a > 0) {
        if (b > 0) {
            System.out.println("Both positive");
        } else {
            System.out.println("a is positive, b is not");
        }
    } else {
        if (b > 0) {
            System.out.println("a is not positive, b is");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Both not positive");
        }
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    String result;
    if (a > 0 && b > 0) {
        result = "Both positive";
    } else if (a > 0) {
        result = "a is positive, b is not";
    } else if (b > 0) {
        result = "a is not positive, b is";
    } else {
        result = "Both not positive";
    }
    System.out.println(result);
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
NCSS（Non-Commenting Source Statements）行数是指代码中的有效行数，不包括注释和空行。过多的NCSS行数可能表明方法或类的复杂性过高。

##### 规则意义
限制方法和类的NCSS行数可以帮助降低复杂性，提高可读性和可维护性，从而减少代码中的缺陷。

##### 错误示例
```java
public void exampleMethod() {
    // 这段代码的NCSS行数超过了限制，表示该方法过于复杂
    int a = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
        a += i;
    }
    System.out.println(a);
    // ...更多逻辑代码...
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public void simpleMethod() {
    int result = calculateSum();
    displayResult(result);
}

private int calculateSum() {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
        sum += i;
    }
    return sum;
}

private void displayResult(int result) {
    System.out.println(result);
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
NCSS (Non-Commenting Source Statements) line count refers to the number of effective lines in the code, excluding comments and blank lines. An excessive NCSS line count may indicate that the method or class is too complex.

##### Rule Significance
Restricting the NCSS line count of methods and classes can help reduce complexity, improve readability and maintainability, thereby reducing defects in the code.

##### Error Example
```java
public void exampleMethod() {
    // The NCSS line count of this code exceeds the limit, indicating that the method is too complex
    int a = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
        a += i;
    }
    System.out.println(a);
    // ...more logic code...
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public void simpleMethod() {
    int result = calculateSum();
    displayResult(result);
}

private int calculateSum() {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
        sum += i;
    }
    return sum;
}

private void displayResult(int result) {
    System.out.println(result);
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，所有类应该被定义在包中。使用无包声明的类会导致代码的可维护性和可读性降低，同时也可能导致类名冲突。

##### 规则意义
定义包可以帮助组织代码，避免命名冲突，并提供更好的访问控制。此外，包的使用有助于代码的模块化和重用。

##### 错误示例
```java
// 无包声明类
public class Example {
    public void doSomething() {
        System.out.println("Doing something...");
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
package com.example;

public class Example {
    public void doSomething() {
        System.out.println("Doing something...");
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, all classes should be defined within a package. Using classes without a package declaration can lead to reduced maintainability and readability of the code, and may also cause class name conflicts.

##### Significance of the Rule
Defining packages helps to organize code, avoid naming conflicts, and provide better access control. Moreover, using packages contributes to the modularity and reusability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
// Class without a package declaration
public class Example {
    public void doSomething() {
        System.out.println("Doing something...");
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
package com.example;

public class Example {
    public void doSomething() {
        System.out.println("Doing something...");
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 `switch` 语句中，建议使用具有区分大小写的标签，以确保代码的清晰性和可维护性。使用非区分大小写的标签可能会导致逻辑错误，特别是在处理字符串值时。

##### 规则意义
使用非区分大小写的标签可能会导致匹配错误，例如在处理用户输入时。如果代码依赖于区分大小写的逻辑，使用非区分大小写的标签可能会导致意外的行为。

##### 错误示例
```java
String value = "Example";
switch (value) {
    case "example":  // 非区分大小写
        System.out.println("Matched!");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Default case");
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
String value = "Example";
switch (value) {
    case "Example":  // 区分大小写
        System.out.println("Matched!");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Default case");
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In `switch` statements, it is recommended to use case-sensitive labels to ensure clarity and maintainability of the code. Using case-insensitive labels may lead to logical errors, especially when handling string values.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using case-insensitive labels can lead to matching errors, such as when processing user input. If the code relies on case-sensitive logic, using case-insensitive labels may result in unexpected behavior.

##### Error Example
```java
String value = "Example";
switch (value) {
    case "example":  // Case-insensitive
        System.out.println("Matched!");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Default case");
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
String value = "Example";
switch (value) {
    case "Example":  // Case-sensitive
        System.out.println("Matched!");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Default case");
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在 Java 中的 switch 语句中使用非区分大小写的标签会导致意外的行为，可能会导致程序逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
使用非区分大小写的标签会使代码在某些情况下难以阅读和维护，容易导致错误的分支执行，从而影响程序的正确性。

##### 错误示例
```java
String input = "value";
switch (input) {
    case "VALUE":  // 错误使用非区分大小写的标签
        System.out.println("Matched case VALUE");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("No match");
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
String input = "value";
switch (input) {
    case "value":  // 正确使用区分大小写的标签
        System.out.println("Matched case value");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("No match");
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
Using case labels that are not case-sensitive in the switch statement in Java can lead to unexpected behavior and may result in logical errors in the program.

##### Rule Meaning
Using case labels that are not case-sensitive makes the code difficult to read and maintain in certain situations, easily leading to incorrect branch executions, thereby affecting the correctness of the program.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
String input = "value";
switch (input) {
    case "VALUE":  // Incorrect use of case-sensitive label
        System.out.println("Matched case VALUE");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("No match");
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
String input = "value";
switch (input) {
    case "value":  // Correct use of case-sensitive label
        System.out.println("Matched case value");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("No match");
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在使用 switch 语句时，如果没有为每个可能的值提供处理逻辑，那么该 switch 语句就是非穷尽的。这会导致在处理未考虑的值时，程序可能出现意外行为。

##### 规则意义
确保 switch 语句涵盖所有可能的情况，以防未处理的情况导致错误或意外行为。这有助于提高代码的可维护性和可预测性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public void processColor(String color) {
    switch (color) {
        case "RED":
            System.out.println("Color is red");
            break;
        case "GREEN":
            System.out.println("Color is green");
            break;
        // 缺少对其他颜色的处理
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public void processColor(String color) {
    switch (color) {
        case "RED":
            System.out.println("Color is red");
            break;
        case "GREEN":
            System.out.println("Color is green");
            break;
        case "BLUE":
            System.out.println("Color is blue");
            break;
        default:
            System.out.println("Unknown color");
            break;
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When using a switch statement, if no handling logic is provided for every possible value, then the switch statement is non-exhaustive. This can lead to unexpected behavior in the program when handling unconsidered values.

##### Rule Significance
Ensure that the switch statement covers all possible cases to prevent unhandled situations from causing errors or unexpected behavior. This helps improve the maintainability and predictability of the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public void processColor(String color) {
    switch (color) {
        case "RED":
            System.out.println("Color is red");
            break;
        case "GREEN":
            System.out.println("Color is green");
            break;
        // Missing handling for other colors
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public void processColor(String color) {
    switch (color) {
        case "RED":
            System.out.println("Color is red");
            break;
        case "GREEN":
            System.out.println("Color is green");
            break;
        case "BLUE":
            System.out.println("Color is blue");
            break;
        default:
            System.out.println("Unknown color");
            break;
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则检查是否存在未实现Serializable接口的类，以避免在需要序列化时出现问题。

##### 规则意义
Java中序列化是将对象转换为字节流，以便将其传输或持久化。未实现Serializable接口的类无法序列化，导致在对象传输或保存时可能会发生异常。实现Serializable接口是确保对象可以安全存储和传输的重要做法。

##### 错误示例
'''java
public class MyClass {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // 此类未实现Serializable接口
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class MyClass implements Serializable {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // 此类实现Serializable接口
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule checks for classes that do not implement the Serializable interface to avoid issues when serialization is required.

##### Rule Importance
Serialization in Java is the process of converting an object into a byte stream for transmission or persistence. Classes that do not implement the Serializable interface cannot be serialized, potentially leading to exceptions during object transmission or storage. Implementing the Serializable interface is an important practice to ensure that objects can be safely stored and transmitted.

##### Error Example
'''java
public class MyClass {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // This class does not implement the Serializable interface
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
import java.io.Serializable;

public class MyClass implements Serializable {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    // This class implements the Serializable interface
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，非静态初始化器可能会导致不必要的复杂性和潜在的错误，尤其是在继承或多线程环境中。建议使用构造函数替代该方式。

##### 规则意义
使用非静态初始化器时，代码的可读性和可维护性降低。此外，它还有可能导致初始化顺序的问题，影响程序的稳定性。采用构造函数可以使代码更加清晰，并且更易于理解和维护。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    {
        // 非静态初始化器
        System.out.println("非静态初始化器");
    }

    public Example() {
        System.out.println("构造函数");
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    public Example() {
        // 在构造函数中进行初始化
        System.out.println("构造函数");
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, non-static initializers can lead to unnecessary complexity and potential errors, especially in inheritance or multithreaded environments. It is recommended to use constructors instead.

##### Rule Meaning
Using non-static initializers reduces the readability and maintainability of the code. Additionally, it may lead to issues with initialization order, affecting the stability of the program. Adopting constructors can make the code clearer and easier to understand and maintain.

##### Error Example
```java
public class Example {
    {
        // Non-static initializer
        System.out.println("Non-static initializer");
    }

    public Example() {
        System.out.println("Constructor");
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    public Example() {
        // Initialization in the constructor
        System.out.println("Constructor");
    }
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在识别非线程安全的单例模式实现。

##### 规则意义
单例模式在多线程环境中可能导致不一致的数据状态。非线程安全的单例实现可能导致多个线程同时创建单例实例，破坏单例的唯一性，从而引发严重错误。

##### 错误示例
'''java
public class NonThreadSafeSingleton {
    private static NonThreadSafeSingleton instance;

    private NonThreadSafeSingleton() {}

    public static NonThreadSafeSingleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new NonThreadSafeSingleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
public class ThreadSafeSingleton {
    private static ThreadSafeSingleton instance;

    private ThreadSafeSingleton() {}

    public static synchronized ThreadSafeSingleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new ThreadSafeSingleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to identify non-thread-safe implementations of the singleton pattern.

##### Rule Significance
The singleton pattern can lead to inconsistent data states in a multithreaded environment. Non-thread-safe singleton implementations may allow multiple threads to create singleton instances simultaneously, violating the uniqueness of the singleton and potentially leading to severe errors.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
public class NonThreadSafeSingleton {
    private static NonThreadSafeSingleton instance;

    private NonThreadSafeSingleton() {}

    public static NonThreadSafeSingleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new NonThreadSafeSingleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
public class ThreadSafeSingleton {
    private static ThreadSafeSingleton instance;

    private ThreadSafeSingleton() {}

    public static synchronized ThreadSafeSingleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new ThreadSafeSingleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
'''

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
此规则旨在确保每个方法中仅有一个返回语句。

##### 规则意义
只有一个返回点可以增强代码的可读性和可维护性。在复杂的方法中，多个返回点可能导致逻辑、状态或资源的管理变得困难，特别是在异常处理时。

##### 错误示例
```java
public int calculate(int num) {
    if (num > 0) {
        return num * 2;
    } else {
        return 0;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public int calculate(int num) {
    int result;
    if (num > 0) {
        result = num * 2;
    } else {
        result = 0;
    }
    return result;
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to ensure that there is only one return statement in each method.

##### Significance of the Rule
Having a single return point can enhance the readability and maintainability of the code. In complex methods, multiple return points can make it difficult to manage logic, state, or resources, especially during exception handling.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public int calculate(int num) {
    if (num > 0) {
        return num * 2;
    } else {
        return 0;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public int calculate(int num) {
    int result;
    if (num > 0) {
        result = num * 2;
    } else {
        result = 0;
    }
    return result;
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，使用集合类（如List）时，调用`toArray()`方法可能不够高效。建议使用相应类型的数组生成器来提高性能。

##### 规则意义
在处理集合时，尤其是大数据量时，使用合适的数组创建方式可以减少不必要的内存分配和复制，提高代码性能。

##### 错误示例
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("Hello");
list.add("World");
String[] array = list.toArray(new String[0]); // 不够优化
```

##### 正确示例
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("Hello");
list.add("World");
String[] array = list.toArray(new String[list.size()]); // 优化后的调用
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, when using collection classes (such as List), calling the `toArray()` method may not be efficient enough. It is recommended to use the corresponding type of array generator to improve performance.

##### Significance of the Rule
When handling collections, especially with large amounts of data, using appropriate array creation methods can reduce unnecessary memory allocation and copying, thereby enhancing code performance.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("Hello");
list.add("World");
String[] array = list.toArray(new String[0]); // Not optimized
```

##### Correct Example
```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("Hello");
list.add("World");
String[] array = list.toArray(new String[list.size()]); // Optimized call
```

