#### 规则概述
在Java中，类如果重写了`equals`方法，那么应该同时重写`hashCode`方法。这是因为在集合中使用`equals`方法来判断对象相等时，哈希码的计算也会受到影响。

##### 规则意义
重写`equals`和`hashCode`方法可以确保集合中的对象能够正确存储和检索。如果只重写了`equals`而未重写`hashCode`，可能导致在哈希表中存储和查找动作不正确。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) return true;
        if (obj == null || getClass() != obj.getClass()) return false;
        Person person = (Person) obj;
        return age == person.age && Objects.equals(name, person.name);
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) return true;
        if (obj == null || getClass() != obj.getClass()) return false;
        Person person = (Person) obj;
        return age == person.age && Objects.equals(name, person.name);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(name, age);
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, if a class overrides the `equals` method, it should also override the `hashCode` method. This is because when using the `equals` method to determine object equality in a collection, the calculation of the hash code will also be affected.

##### Significance of the Rule
Overriding the `equals` and `hashCode` methods ensures that objects in a collection can be stored and retrieved correctly. If `equals` is overridden but `hashCode` is not, it may lead to incorrect storage and lookup in a hash table.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) return true;
        if (obj == null || getClass() != obj.getClass()) return false;
        Person person = (Person) obj;
        return age == person.age && Objects.equals(name, person.name);
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Person {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object obj) {
        if (this == obj) return true;
        if (obj == null || getClass() != obj.getClass()) return false;
        Person person = (Person) obj;
        return age == person.age && Objects.equals(name, person.name);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(name, age);
    }
}
```

