rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则旨在检测使用单一方法定义单例模式的类，这种实现方式虽然简洁，但易导致不必要的复杂性和潜在的线程问题。

##### 规则意义
正确实现单例模式可以确保在整个应用程序中仅有一个实例被创建，避免资源的浪费和线程安全问题。使用单一方法定义单例可能导致在多线程应用程序中产生不确定性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static synchronized Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```
这里的正确示例通过使用 `synchronized` 关键字来保证线程安全性，确保在多线程环境下只有一个实例被创建。

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to detect classes that define the singleton pattern using a single method. While this implementation is simple, it can lead to unnecessary complexity and potential threading issues.

##### Significance of the Rule
Properly implementing the singleton pattern ensures that only one instance is created throughout the application, avoiding resource wastage and threading safety issues. Using a single method to define a singleton may lead to uncertainties in multi-threaded applications.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static synchronized Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }
}
```
The correct example here ensures thread safety by using the `synchronized` keyword, ensuring that only one instance is created in a multi-threaded environment.

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则检测那些被声明为单例的类中存在返回新实例的方法。这种设计违反了单例模式的原则，可能导致多个实例的创建。

##### 规则意义
单例模式的核心思想是确保一个类只有一个实例，并提供全局访问点。如果单例类返回新的实例，将导致无法控制实例的数量，破坏单例的单一性，增加资源消耗和潜在的逻辑错误。

##### 错误示例
'''java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }

    public Singleton createNewInstance() {
        return new Singleton(); // 错误：返回了一个新实例
    }
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance; // 正确：只返回单一实例
    }
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule detects methods that return new instances within classes that are declared as singletons. This design violates the principles of the singleton pattern and may lead to the creation of multiple instances.

##### Rule Meaning
The core idea of the singleton pattern is to ensure that a class has only one instance and provides a global access point. If a singleton class returns new instances, it will lead to an uncontrolled number of instances, undermining the uniqueness of the singleton, increasing resource consumption, and introducing potential logical errors.

##### Wrong Example
'''java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance;
    }

    public Singleton createNewInstance() {
        return new Singleton(); // Error: returns a new instance
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
public class Singleton {
    private static Singleton instance;

    private Singleton() {}

    public static Singleton getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new Singleton();
        }
        return instance; // Correct: only returns the single instance
    }
}
'''

