#### 规则概述
在多线程环境中，使用`HashMap`可能导致数据不一致和并发问题，建议使用`ConcurrentHashMap`来保障线程安全。

##### 规则意义
`ConcurrentHashMap`比`HashMap`更适合在多线程环境中使用，能够在保证线程安全的同时提供更好的性能。

##### 错误示例
```java
Map<String, String> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("key1", "value1");

// 多线程环境下可能导致数据不一致
new Thread(() -> map.put("key2", "value2")).start();
new Thread(() -> System.out.println(map.get("key1"))).start();
```

##### 正确示例
```java
Map<String, String> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
map.put("key1", "value1");

// 正确使用ConcurrentHashMap在多线程环境下进行操作
new Thread(() -> map.put("key2", "value2")).start();
new Thread(() -> System.out.println(map.get("key1"))).start();
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In a multithreaded environment, using `HashMap` may lead to data inconsistency and concurrency issues. It is recommended to use `ConcurrentHashMap` to ensure thread safety.

##### Rule Significance
`ConcurrentHashMap` is more suitable for use in multithreaded environments than `HashMap`, as it provides better performance while ensuring thread safety.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
Map<String, String> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("key1", "value1");

// May lead to data inconsistency in a multithreaded environment
new Thread(() -> map.put("key2", "value2")).start();
new Thread(() -> System.out.println(map.get("key1"))).start();
```

##### Correct Example
```java
Map<String, String> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
map.put("key1", "value1");

// Correctly using ConcurrentHashMap for operations in a multithreaded environment
new Thread(() -> map.put("key2", "value2")).start();
new Thread(() -> System.out.println(map.get("key1"))).start();
```

