#### 规则概述
在Java中，记录异常时需确保使用正确的日志记录方式，以便于后续的调试和排错。在记录异常信息时，应保持异常堆栈的完整性，并避免记录不必要的敏感信息。

##### 规则意义
正确的异常日志记录有助于开发者快速定位问题，避免遗漏重要的异常信息。同时，遵循相关的安全最佳实践，防止将敏感数据暴露在日志中。

##### 错误示例
'''java
try {
    // Some code that may throw an exception
    int result = 10 / 0;
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("An error occurred: " + e.getMessage()); // 错误的日志记录方式
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
try {
    // Some code that may throw an exception
    int result = 10 / 0;
} catch (Exception e) {
    logger.error("An error occurred:", e); // 正确的日志记录方式，包含完整的堆栈信息
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, when logging exceptions, it is essential to use the correct logging approach to facilitate subsequent debugging and troubleshooting. When logging exception information, the integrity of the exception stack should be maintained, and unnecessary sensitive information should be avoided.

##### Significance of the Rule
Proper exception logging helps developers quickly locate issues and prevents the omission of important exception information. At the same time, following relevant security best practices prevents the exposure of sensitive data in logs.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
try {
    // Some code that may throw an exception
    int result = 10 / 0;
} catch (Exception e) {
    System.out.println("An error occurred: " + e.getMessage()); // Incorrect logging method
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
try {
    // Some code that may throw an exception
    int result = 10 / 0;
} catch (Exception e) {
    logger.error("An error occurred:", e); // Correct logging method, includes complete stack information
}
'''

