rules.content:
#### 规则概述
应使用try-with-resources语句来处理资源的自动关闭，以避免资源泄露。

##### 规则意义
使用try-with-resources确保在使用完资源（如文件、数据库连接等）后自动关闭它们，减少内存泄漏和资源浪费的风险。

##### 错误示例
```java
FileInputStream inputStream = null;
try {
    inputStream = new FileInputStream("file.txt");
    // 进行文件读取操作
} catch (IOException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
} finally {
    if (inputStream != null) {
        try {
            inputStream.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
try (FileInputStream inputStream = new FileInputStream("file.txt")) {
    // 进行文件读取操作
} catch (IOException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
The try-with-resources statement should be used to handle automatic resource closing to avoid resource leaks.

##### Rule Significance
Using try-with-resources ensures that resources (such as files, database connections, etc.) are automatically closed after use, reducing the risk of memory leaks and resource wastage.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
FileInputStream inputStream = null;
try {
    inputStream = new FileInputStream("file.txt");
    // Perform file reading operations
} catch (IOException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
} finally {
    if (inputStream != null) {
        try {
            inputStream.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
try (FileInputStream inputStream = new FileInputStream("file.txt")) {
    // Perform file reading operations
} catch (IOException e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

