#### 规则概述
该规则建议使用可变参数（varargs）来提高方法的灵活性与可读性。

##### 规则意义
使用可变参数可以避免过多的方法重载，使代码更简洁。引入可变参数可以提高方法的调用效率以及参数的传递灵活性。

##### 错误示例
'''java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    System.out.println(a);
    System.out.println(b);
}

exampleMethod(1, 2);
exampleMethod(1, 2, 3);
'''

##### 正确示例
'''java
public void exampleMethod(int... numbers) {
    for (int number : numbers) {
        System.out.println(number);
    }
}

exampleMethod(1);
exampleMethod(1, 2, 3);
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule recommends using variable arguments (varargs) to enhance the flexibility and readability of methods.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using variable arguments can avoid excessive method overloading, making the code more concise. Introducing variable arguments can improve method call efficiency and the flexibility of parameter passing.

##### Incorrect Example
'''java
public void exampleMethod(int a, int b) {
    System.out.println(a);
    System.out.println(b);
}

exampleMethod(1, 2);
exampleMethod(1, 2, 3);
'''

##### Correct Example
'''java
public void exampleMethod(int... numbers) {
    for (int number : numbers) {
        System.out.println(number);
    }
}

exampleMethod(1);
exampleMethod(1, 2, 3);
'''

