#### 规则概述
当一个方法在子类中被覆盖时，如果覆盖的方法并没有实现任何新的功能或逻辑，只是简单地调用父类的方法，那么这个覆盖方法是无用的。

##### 规则意义
使用无用的覆盖方法会导致代码冗余，增加了代码的复杂性，同时可能会让其他开发者产生误解。应避免这种情况，以保持代码的简洁性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
```java
class Parent {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent Show");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    void show() {
        super.show(); // 无用的覆盖方法
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
class Parent {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent Show");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    // Child class does not override show()
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
When a method is overridden in a subclass, if the overriding method does not implement any new functionality or logic but merely calls the parent class's method, then this overriding method is considered useless.

##### Significance of the Rule
Using useless overriding methods can lead to code redundancy, increase complexity, and may cause misunderstandings among other developers. This situation should be avoided to maintain code simplicity and readability.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
class Parent {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent Show");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    void show() {
        super.show(); // Useless overriding method
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
class Parent {
    void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent Show");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    // Child class does not override show()
}
```

rules.content:
#### 规则概述
在Java中，使用`this`关键字引用当前类时，如果已在同一类上下文中，使用`Qualified`的方式（即`this.this`）是多余的。

##### 规则意义
这种冗余的代码不仅没有任何实际意义，还会降低代码的可读性和简洁性。清晰的代码能够提高维护性和可读性。

##### 错误示例
```java
public class Example {
    private int value;

    public void setValue(int value) {
        this.value = value;  // 正确用法
        this.this.value = value; // 错误用法: 多余的限定符
    }
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
public class Example {
    private int value;

    public void setValue(int value) {
        this.value = value; // 正确用法
    }
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
In Java, when using the `this` keyword to reference the current class, it is redundant to use the `Qualified` way (i.e., `this.this`) if already in the same class context.

##### Rule Significance
This redundant code not only serves no practical purpose, but also decreases the readability and conciseness of the code. Clear code can enhance maintainability and readability.

##### Incorrect Example
```java
public class Example {
    private int value;

    public void setValue(int value) {
        this.value = value;  // Correct usage
        this.this.value = value; // Incorrect usage: redundant qualifier
    }
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
public class Example {
    private int value;

    public void setValue(int value) {
        this.value = value; // Correct usage
    }
}
```

