#### 规则概述
该规则旨在防止在while循环中使用字面量布尔值作为循环条件。直接使用`true`或`false`作为条件的while循环可能导致无限循环或逻辑错误。

##### 规则意义
使用字面量布尔值作为循环条件会使代码的意图不明确，增加代码的维护难度和出错几率。我们应该使用可读性更强且易于调试的条件表达式。

##### 错误示例
```java
while (true) {
    // 执行某些逻辑
}
```

##### 正确示例
```java
boolean condition = true;
while (condition) {
    // 执行某些逻辑
    // 根据某些条件可能会改变condition的值
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule aims to prevent the use of literal boolean values as loop conditions in while loops. Using `true` or `false` directly as the condition of a while loop can lead to infinite loops or logical errors.

##### Rule Significance
Using literal boolean values as loop conditions makes the code's intent unclear, increasing the difficulty of code maintenance and the likelihood of errors. We should use more readable and easily debuggable conditional expressions.

##### Error Example
```java
while (true) {
    // Perform some logic
}
```

##### Correct Example
```java
boolean condition = true;
while (condition) {
    // Perform some logic
    // The value of condition may change based on certain conditions
}
```
